## solution

#### using a hashmap (object)

```js
const pairProduct = (numbers, targetProduct) => {
  const previousNums = {};
  for (let i = 0; i < numbers.length; i += 1) {
    const num = numbers[i];
    const complement = targetProduct / num;

    if (complement in previousNums) return [ previousNums[complement], i ];

    previousNums[num] = i;
  }
};

```

- n = length of array
- Time: O(n)
- Space: O(n)

